 1115|  2.61k|#if defined(__GNUC__) && defined(__x86_64__)
 1116|       |        /* Align the decompression loop to 32 + 16 bytes.
 1117|       |         *
 1118|       |         * zstd compiled with gcc-9 on an Intel i9-9900k shows 10% decompression
 1119|       |         * speed swings based on the alignment of the decompression loop. This
 1120|       |         * performance swing is caused by parts of the decompression loop falling
 1121|       |         * out of the DSB. The entire decompression loop should fit in the DSB,
 1122|       |         * when it can't we get much worse performance. You can measure if you've
 1123|       |         * hit the good case or the bad case with this perf command for some
 1124|       |         * compressed file test.zst:
 1125|       |         *
 1126|       |         *   perf stat -e cycles -e instructions -e idq.all_dsb_cycles_any_uops \
 1127|       |         *             -e idq.all_mite_cycles_any_uops -- ./zstd -tq test.zst
 1128|       |         *
 1129|       |         * If you see most cycles served out of the MITE you've hit the bad case.
 1130|       |         * If you see most cycles served out of the DSB you've hit the good case.
 1131|       |         * If it is pretty even then you may be in an okay case.
 1132|       |         *
 1133|       |         * This issue has been reproduced on the following CPUs:
 1134|       |         *   - Kabylake: Macbook Pro (15-inch, 2019) 2.4 GHz Intel Core i9
 1135|       |         *               Use Instruments->Counters to get DSB/MITE cycles.
 1136|       |         *               I never got performance swings, but I was able to
 1137|       |         *               go from the good case of mostly DSB to half of the
 1138|       |         *               cycles served from MITE.
 1139|       |         *   - Coffeelake: Intel i9-9900k
 1140|       |         *   - Coffeelake: Intel i7-9700k
 1141|       |         *
 1142|       |         * I haven't been able to reproduce the instability or DSB misses on any
 1143|       |         * of the following CPUS:
 1144|       |         *   - Haswell
 1145|       |         *   - Broadwell: Intel(R) Xeon(R) CPU E5-2680 v4 @ 2.40GH
 1146|       |         *   - Skylake
 1147|       |         *
 1148|       |         * If you are seeing performance stability this script can help test.
 1149|       |         * It tests on 4 commits in zstd where I saw performance change.
 1150|       |         *
 1151|       |         *   https://gist.github.com/terrelln/9889fc06a423fd5ca6e99351564473f4
 1152|       |         */
